# Running experiments and contributing upstream

- **Read `INSTRUCTIONS.local.md` before running anything.** It is the single source of truth for
  hosts, ports, relay start commands and their gotchas, locating freshly built binaries, clips, rig
  scripts and graders. When an environment fact changes, update it there (facts only, no findings).
- Consult `lab/method-notes.md` when designing or grading an experiment; fix the pass criteria in the
  experiment's `lab/test-*.md` before the first run.
- Never edit a rig script while a run uses it.
- **Before pushing to an upstream repository, pass that repository's gate, not ours.** For `moq-dev`:
  `just fix`, then `just check`, from the worktree (`INSTRUCTIONS.local.md` §1). Its conventions
  differ from ours (its `.editorconfig` indents shell with spaces; `lab/scripts/` uses tabs); re-run
  any script its formatter rewrote before pushing it.
- Post nothing upstream (issues, comments, pull requests) without the author's go-ahead.
